{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno","id":1551850,"title":"Albrecht's inferno","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-24T20:12:54-07:00","id":1551850,"title":"Albrecht's inferno","content":"SoI got a possibility stupid idea.... Everyone knows how W5 reduced pastehtic bitter shell of a man and how the whole world has become a hell for him.<br /> <br /> Well then what if it is a hell? What if the world he's in is actually a hell?<br /> <br /> What if the whole world presented in w5 is a lie created by the Wyrm as both a means to turn the king of the garous over to the wrym point of view and as a means of petty revenge. <br /> <br /> Some how the nation has that fact and has dispatch a group of the best warriors of they generation to rescue the king from his coner of hell...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-24T21:15:52-07:00","id":1551852,"title":"","content":"It would be metatextually more in line with Zapathasura using Chimerstry 10 to make everything more like Vampire. Which, of course, results in a false world that every fiber in the being of every Garou and Fera tells them to resist and reject. The &quot;Apocalypse&quot; at the end of W5 would then result in a signature character uttering the phrase of &quot;anywhere can be heaven, as long as you try to live,&quot; turning the vampires to tang, and emerging into the true WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-25T06:18:07-07:00","id":1551855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno#post1551850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SoI got a possibility stupid idea.... Everyone knows how W5 reduced pastehtic bitter shell of a man and how the whole world has become a hell for him.<br /> <br /> Well then what if it is a hell? What if the world he's in is actually a hell?<br /> <br /> What if the whole world presented in w5 is a lie created by the Wyrm as both a means to turn the king of the garous over to the wrym point of view and as a means of petty revenge.<br /> <br /> Some how the nation has that fact and has dispatch a group of the best warriors of they generation to rescue the king from his coner of hell...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting and fascinating idea, but how did the nation realize the whole world is a lie focused on Albrecht? And how can you stop whatever it is that can turn the entire world into a hell for singular creature? This is not a problem that you can punch your way if you just had enough muscle, as described in the premise the best warriors are actually less useful than the best scholars and mystics.<br /> <br /> You are actually describing something close to (but not exactly like) Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-25-2025, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-25T06:33:11-07:00","id":1551856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1551855#post1551855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not a problem that you can punch your way if you just had enough muscle.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, in Werewolf, despite how combat-centric game it is... basically nothing, literally nothing could be solved by punching your way through the problem<br /> Interestingly enough the Rokea - walking powerhouses with jaws who easly could snap a Garou in two with a bite - summarized this perfectly:<br /> <br /> &quot;No, dirtwalker, I do not exaggerate. Some she told to make her laugh, some she told to sing songs, but most she told to fight. One race, the most famous (among your kind) race of Changers, she created to be her army against the Unmaking.<br /> They would fight against the Unmaking as long as they all lived, and they would turn back the tides of destruction.<br /> Naive. Foolish. Arrogant. Impossible.<br /> The Unmaking can no more be turned back with an army than can a tsunami.<br /> But her army was there, nonetheless, and they needed something to fight. And in the absence of some great creature that would bring on the end of all things, they fought the other Changers.<br /> (\u2026)<br /> We found it terribly funny that these creatures, who lived on such a small part of the world, felt they could turn back the Unmaking, no matter how great their fury or how sharp their claws.&quot;<br /> <br /> And at the end of the day... it is true, painfully true<br /> What the Garou could achive with muscle is band-aid at best but they - like a bad doctor - rearly or never solve the cause, just the symptoms of a problem<br /> It not really completely the Garou's fault 'tho - the Spirits encouraged their &quot;bad&quot; behaviour most of the time. Or the Garou behaviour shaped the spirits and thr world around them, who knows?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-25T11:41:21-07:00","id":1551861,"title":"","content":"I don't really see the Rokea book as worth keeping around for a number of reasons. Not in its current form, written by the author that it was. Also, that take is painfully Chimerstry 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-25T13:12:08-07:00","id":1551862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno#post1551850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the whole world presented in w5 is a lie created by the Wyrm as both a means to turn the king of the garous over to the wrym point of view and as a means of petty revenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I was going to implement something like that, I'd probably use the Dream Zone in some kind of way. The affected Garou are in some kind of mass common dream. It could be only that the Garou are only impacted while they sleep, and you tell the story as essentially one single mass dream (no matter how long the dream appears to take - years, even decades, can go by in a single dream). Or possibly even the Garou who are awake are &quot;trapped&quot; in a type of shadow play like the level four Galliard gift Shadows by the Firelight. In either case, to use your scenario, the key to resolving this is in Albrecht's head - perhaps this is a nightmare generated by his unconscious mind (probably under pressure of a powerful Wyrm dream being).<br /> <br /> The plot would be some mix of the Matrix, Inception, and Nightmare on Elm Street.<br /> <br /> The big baddie behind it would be some powerful Wyrm aligned being in the Dream Zone invading Gaia's dream/reality. Presumably the help of Chimera would be instrumental in fixing the problem. In Garou cosmology, dreams are the forerunner of reality so the failure to stop this mass dream/delusion will eventually allow it to turn reality into the nightmare.<br /> <br /> That's probably how I would try to run something like this.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-25T13:40:52-07:00","id":1551863,"title":"","content":"It has occurred to me that depicting WW5th as a setting that explores what happens when The Apocalypse <i>never ends</i> might be as logical approach as any - a way of illustrating why \u201csometimes it\u2019s better to burn out than fade away\u201d (Heck, one could use it as a grim portent to fuel Garou willingness to march onto the Battleground for their Last Battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-26T14:21:53-07:00","id":1551877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1551855#post1551855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Interesting and fascinating idea, but how did the nation realize the whole world is a lie focused on Albrecht? And how can you stop whatever it is that can turn the entire world into a hell for singular creature? This is not a problem that you can punch your way if you just had enough muscle, as described in the premise the best warriors are actually less useful than the best scholars and mystics.<br /> <br /> You are actually describing something close to (but not exactly like) Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honstly I was thinking more that he's simply trapped in a pocket realm in the deep umbra ratherthanthe more esoteric takes on his situation. Not that there's anything wrong with that of course. <br /> <br /> He would have been Spirited Away during the chaos of a important battle. Or maybe it's a simullar situation to By Night Studios version of WtA where he trapped himself in the umbra as a desperate sacrifice to seal a stong bane to stop/delay the apcolypse, if there's any time for the forces of the wyrm to seal him into a hell it's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-27T20:16:23-07:00","id":1551889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1551856#post1551856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, in Werewolf, despite how combat-centric game it is... basically nothing, literally nothing could be solved by punching your way through the problem</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> I am by no means familiar with ALL the lore, but most of the problems seem to be either coordination problems with the whole humanity, or better solved by mental and social power: blowing Pentex plants and killing Fomori might feel great, both as a player and as a character, but lobbying for stronger enviromental laws and the enforcement of those laws would hurt the Wyrm more AND help Gaia more. Inventing cleaner and cheaper systems of energy generation and distribution would decontaminate faster than destroying oil plants.<br /> <br /> And those are just top of my head, of course we come into the suspension of disbelief that most of these games require and the setting premises to make it an entertaining game. It is not meant to be a faithful representation of reality otherwise it would not be fun... But people enjoy playing <b>Werewolf the Apocalypse</b> as righteous face punchers, very few would love adventures in <b>Werewolf the Environmental-Social-Governance Lobbying</b> as scientists, environmental researchers or class action lawyers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-28-2025, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-01T22:26:56-07:00","id":1551984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1551889#post1551889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf the Environmental-Social-Governance Lobbying</b> as scientists, environmental researchers or class action lawyers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough this is the end goal of the Eastern Concordat faction from By Nights Studio Version of WtA from what I understand when reading about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Eastcons happily use the information and power they wield to hold space for humans, especially those who could deeply impact the world around them. This faction urges a stronger and more thorough integration of Kinfolk into Garou society as warriors, healers, and visionaries, much like the Dawn Tribes. They do not want to hide their Kinfolk away, keeping them from the world with the excuse of protecting them.<br /> <br /> Instead, Eastern Concordat members wish to teach and prepare their Kinfolk, giving them knowledge and tools to take a more active role in the world in which they live, embracing the ways and guidance of the Hearthbound to integrate kin into their societies. Through their kin, the Eastern Concordat actively seeks influence in the mortal halls of power, leveraging humanity itself to benefit Gaia and all her children. Eastcons believe that keeping up with the modern era is of import. Stagnation is another form of corruption, and by refusing to change with the world around them, the Garou have let this corruption take root and fester. Only by learning and growing can they embody the balance they seek to forge anew in the Triat. </div> </div> </div>(Just to Note the above is from WtE which uses BNS lore as a foundation for it's setting wold probably be some differentence from BNS lore.)<br /> <br /> Like they whole thing is wanting the garou to make a effort to understand humanity more (primarily by not treating they kinfolk as trash) so they could more easily influence them to take a more gaian view. Like sure they probably would still murder pentex executives but it's just one tool in a wider toolbox rather than the only tool.<br /> <br /> ... Moving back on topic I wonder how Albrecht would feel when he's rescued from his hell. Like as far as he knows the nation failed and collapsed but not only did a group of garous kicked down the door to tell him no this is wrong but go on to say the whole world is actually a illusion. Like from his presumptive this whole thing is massive whiplash for him.<br /> <br /> Like the whole thing is Compatible to Don Quixote pt 2 ending with King Arthur busting into Don's bed room just as he was about to accept reality to say that no the whole story up to this point is actually illusion castled on him by the lotus eaters and there's still quests for him to do, he then promply swoop him off his deathbed and ride off into the sun set...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 07-02-2025, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T07:49:47-07:00","id":1552144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1551889#post1551889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed.<br /> <br /> I am by no means familiar with ALL the lore, but most of the problems seem to be either coordination problems with the whole humanity, or better solved by mental and social power: blowing Pentex plants and killing Fomori might feel great, both as a player and as a character, but lobbying for stronger enviromental laws and the enforcement of those laws would hurt the Wyrm more AND help Gaia more. Inventing cleaner and cheaper systems of energy generation and distribution would decontaminate faster than destroying oil plants.<br /> <br /> And those are just top of my head, of course we come into the suspension of disbelief that most of these games require and the setting premises to make it an entertaining game. It is not meant to be a faithful representation of reality otherwise it would not be fun... But people enjoy playing <b>Werewolf the Apocalypse</b> as righteous face punchers, very few would love adventures in <b>Werewolf the Environmental-Social-Governance Lobbying</b> as scientists, environmental researchers or class action lawyers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my personal hell... I'm a biologist, and became az biologist because werewolf the apocalypse. It's my first rpg and the books just put me in the ambiental cause. The more I studied and delved into the subject, the less I saw how the Garou War could be won the way it is fought. Obviously, it is not a lost battle as the books want to make it seem. This vision of an apocalyptic and hopeless future is just capitalism trying to convince us that there is no life outside of it and that we have to keep the system as it is. But, nowadays, I have had more and more difficulty in coming up with ideas for chronicles to narrate... simply, all the ideas are either out of touch with reality or I don't see them as convincing or that they will make any difference in the outcome of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T10:54:28-07:00","id":1552148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1552144#post1552144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's my personal hell... I'm a biologist, and became az biologist because werewolf the apocalypse. It's my first rpg and the books just put me in the ambiental cause. The more I studied and delved into the subject, the less I saw how the Garou War could be won the way it is fought. Obviously, it is not a lost battle as the books want to make it seem. This vision of an apocalyptic and hopeless future is just capitalism trying to convince us that there is no life outside of it and that we have to keep the system as it is. But, nowadays, I have had more and more difficulty in coming up with ideas for chronicles to narrate... simply, all the ideas are either out of touch with reality or I don't see them as convincing or that they will make any difference in the outcome of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that WtA is also about adding a layer of supernatural conspiracies to the matter, and passes in a fictional world, where not everything follows what would make sense in the real world.<br /> <br /> Focus on the supernatural side. Also, on the things that happen in their lives as a whole. Not every, or even most, plots need to be about fighting the Wyrm and/or saving the environment.<br /> <br /> And some stories more focused on being political and interfering from the shadows (as they can't do much directly because of Rage) may be a good change of pace. Also, stories about Sept politics precisely to show the other Garou the error of trying to solve everything through poorly aimed violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T17:17:12-07:00","id":1552177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1552144#post1552144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The more I studied and delved into the subject, the less I saw how the Garou War could be won the way it is fought.</b> Obviously, it is not a lost battle as the books want to make it seem. This vision of an apocalyptic and hopeless future is just capitalism trying to convince us that there is no life outside of it and that we have to keep the system as it is. But, nowadays, I have had more and more difficulty in coming up with ideas for chronicles to narrate... simply, all the ideas are either out of touch with reality or I don't see them as convincing or that they will make any difference in the outcome of things.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> gave great ideas on how to create chronicles.<br /> <br /> And to repeat myself, this is a game, willing suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> Be aware that at the time the writers did not have access to the trove of information that we take for granted today with the internet. Most of the writers for White Wolf were amateurs building with great passion (but lacking lots of real world knowledge) regarding the topics, and that includes game design, that gave certain cultural insensitivities (metis, kuei-jin, etc) and some wonky mechanics. Today RPG writers as group have learned from those mistakes and build better systems and more compelling cultural content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T02:51:44-07:00","id":1552191,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d argue that the Garou way of war AS IT CURRENTLY EXISTS being increasingly inadequate to the task of averting the Apocalypse is, in fact, deliberately implicit to the game line - because it makes the Younger Generation, who are better able to spot the faults inherent in the system and lack incentive to stick with that system because it works for THEM far more important than they would be in a Garou Nation that worked without gratuitous faults (Given the Tribes tend to value age &amp; experience, since these tend to bring power, personal and institutional).<br /> <br /> The fact that the average PC Garou, unlike the average PC Kindred, actually have a solid shot at acquiring real power and influence in a relatively short time span (Given werewolves are NOT ageless and given the turnover rate of personnel in the Apocalypse War) makes it even more credible that this year\u2019s pups might be next year\u2019s celebrated reformer.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, this approach certainly offers a wealth of interesting challenges to those hungry for some good roleplaying and hungry to make a difference in the hairier regions of the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T06:30:29-07:00","id":1552196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1552191#post1552191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d argue that the Garou way of war AS IT CURRENTLY EXISTS being increasingly inadequate to the task of averting the Apocalypse is, in fact, deliberately implicit to the game line - because it makes the Younger Generation, who are better able to spot the faults inherent in the system and lack incentive to stick with that system because it works for THEM far more important than they would be in a Garou Nation that worked without gratuitous faults (Given the Tribes tend to value age &amp; experience, since these tend to bring power, personal and institutional).<br /> <br /> The fact that the average PC Garou, unlike the average PC Kindred, actually have a solid shot at acquiring real power and influence in a relatively short time span (Given werewolves are NOT ageless and given the turnover rate of personnel in the Apocalypse War) makes it even more credible that this year\u2019s pups might be next year\u2019s celebrated reformer.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, this approach certainly offers a wealth of interesting challenges to those hungry for some good roleplaying and hungry to make a difference in the hairier regions of the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what? I had not thought it that way before, and yes, the new-generation-doing-things-differently could be the answer to the structural issues. <br /> <br /> Fighting tooth and claw is the easy way, it is also the losing way. If the Garou as a whole can learn this, they have a shot at winning. That would be a Ragabash hero role to contrast with the Ahroun ideal of the war leader that tribes have, or the Philodox during peace times. That was something that I liked about Forsaken, there your auspice did not set what you did, but how you did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-08-2025, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-09T05:55:30-07:00","id":1552228,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s nice to know that FORSAKEN and APOCALYPSE have their own takes on things: I\u2019m also pleased that my suggestion was helpful and am confident that you\u2019ll put the notion to good use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-11T10:21:28-07:00","id":1552287,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the tips! The ideia of a Ragabash hero is very cool, because in my experience it's the most common choice of auspices (second been Theurge).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-26T01:36:04-07:00","id":1554019,"title":"","content":"So I found a amusing post on another forum that's tangentially related to the main topic to this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like the patches from people who actually wanted to make something good, so I have it that W5 is the result of a powerful Bane of Fake News awakening after remnants of the Swords of Heimdall went full tantrum-traitor and sold out to the BSD. Some elements are real, but a lot is bullshit and Sword wishcasting about how they think the world should work, having decided that Garou should engage in constant self-loathing until Hauglosk convinces them the Swords were right. It's literally the alt-right version of the Garou, and doing any good despite the delusions inflicted on them is remarkable.<br /> <br /> Next edition involves the actual Get cutting one of its throats, causing other Garou to snap out of the delirium and realize the reason the Stargazers were being aloof was because they weren't affected and talking to a maddened Black Fury was like conversing with someone with advanced Alzheimer's. It's upsetting and you know you can't help. </div> </div> </div>I doubt that White wolf would go with that as justification for w6 getting another setting reboot nor would they actually make a 6th ed in first place. But if they did it's going to elect some wild Reactions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T05:50:16-07:00","id":1554055,"title":"","content":"I watched a video in the channel William SRD in youtube (I totally recoomend it's channel) about the possibilities to world of darkness future... one of the paths him analisy is the total reboot (again) and focus in a new &quot;goth-punk&quot; scenario witrh the rebellious think of the present days, instead just denounce the things are bad, given answers too. I like of the ideas present there. But, I'm also the Paradox go to the sameway the another midias corporation today: the safe way. Just repeat which is safe to profit quickly and move on, without give anything really new or inovation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T09:42:41-07:00","id":1554059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1554055#post1554055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one of the paths him analisy is the total reboot (again) and focus in a new &quot;goth-punk&quot; scenario witrh the rebellious think of the present days, instead just denounce the things are bad, given answers too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that this is exactly how we got W5 in the first place, regardless if we don't like how Paradox did it.<br /> <br /> Werewolf isn't Goth-Punk and never has been, to begin with. Paradox thought instead of rolling with the game as is, they were smarter than the game's actual fan-base and could make it better by making it more Vampire. They recreated the setting following their own ideas of what the game should be without any regard for what people who already liked the game think.<br /> <br /> Paradox's whole mess comes from forcing into the game their own limited views of what's the right way of being WoD. Which was already a disaster for Vampire, but was even worse for a game that, lo and behold, <b>isn't Vampire</b>.<br /> <br /> How do you expect to tackle the problem with the same attitude and get another result? You can do marginally better by not being as moronic in many issues as they are, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> I'm all in for bringing back the old, pre-5th ed, setting. I'm also all in for keeping the current setting and doing with it the best we can, as it has its own fans, unless <b>those fans</b> want something else. Just ignoring the current fan base seems to me like making the same mistake again out of spite, and this very thread is proof that at least sometimes that's exactly that. Now, trying to &quot;solve&quot; the current setting by doing the very same path again?<br /> <br /> For whatever it's worth, a similar but more respectful take is also exactly what the <i>New World of Darkness</i>, currently <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, is. If the idea is to just have a brand new setting, this boat sailed 20 years ago and did very well, except for the strong resistance of cWoD fans who wouldn't change settings at any cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T17:15:55-07:00","id":1554068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1554059#post1554059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, trying to &quot;solve&quot; the current setting by doing the very same path again?<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>We honestly there's a simple soution to that. Crater to the lancer Fans of cause! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But really this post by one of Lancers Main author is a great foundation for any future WtA games. <br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/OgfETFq.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/OgfETFq.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/OgfETFq.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Honestly what we need is more straight forward optimistic story without the bitter irony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T17:37:26-07:00","id":1554069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1554068#post1554068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly what we need is more straight forward optimistic story without the bitter irony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Original WtA is already far more optimistic than most WoD to begin with, as it has the possibility of an actual victory baked in, but setting this apart...<br /> <br /> How does this really solves anything? I can see how it creates an interesting new setting that can be considered an inheritor of the old setting, but how does it actually gives either pre-5 or W5 fans a game they want to play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T18:18:15-07:00","id":1554070,"title":"","content":"The WoD does not need another edition, and likely wouldn't need another anniversary rehaul for a long time. Its philosophy was really more in line with having a spiritual sequel; an effort by fans influenced by it, turned game designers, to hit a lot of the notes of the WoD games, tweaked to also account for the new creators' points of view and what's important to them.<br /> <br /> Continuing the WoD on with new editions is even more corporate a decision than the nakedly terrible corporate reason for buying the IP from CCP is, because someone thought that Bloodlines 2 would be a slam dunk and gateway into their own Marvel EU, only to find that nothing was so easy, especially when you hire people who kind of hate every part of said universe but Vampire and think that it absolutely needs to be more like Vampire.<br /> <br /> The WoD is dead. It died in 2004 with the Time of Judgment. The 20th anniversary editions were just a QOL and equivalent of old games ported to new platforms to archive the experience for the future. We should all learn to move on and utilize bits of it in new games with new settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T22:06:06-07:00","id":1554073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1554070#post1554070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The WoD is dead. It died in 2004 with the Time of Judgment. The 20th anniversary editions were just a QOL and equivalent of old games ported to new platforms to archive the experience for the future. We should all learn to move on and utilize bits of it in new games with new settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't go so far. I mean, I think you're mostly right, but I don't think a new edition is completely out of question. I used to think like that, but the success of WoD20th said otherwise.<br /> <br /> As out of pace with the current world as it is, WoD still has a lot of traction. And while the QoL changes in WoD20 to date are mostly welcome, I think the <i>mechanics</i> did deserve a new edition after WoD20 was complete. I'd be wary of any metaplot advance, but the game surely could use new rules that are actually good for a change.<br /> <br /> Some lines can particularly benefit of this. the Big Three VWM have been explored to exhaustion, but other lines still had a lot of room for exploration and fans that really wanted to see it happen.<br /> <br /> Now, in my opinion a proper continuation past-End Times would fit well in this idea of new games. Paradox's most glaring mistake was to not really commit to following through with the End Times scenarios and build whole new games using the old lore, but based on new ideas.<br /> <br /> Other than that... as I said, that's CoD. It's a good game. Actually, a great game. Unfortunately, it's also the living proof that people don't want a new game, they want WoD, and I don't think making a New New WoD will change this unless it is somehow a continuation of the cWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T22:36:42-07:00","id":1554074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1554073#post1554073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't go so far. I mean, I think you're mostly right, but I don't think a new edition is completely out of question. I used to think like that, but the success of WoD20th said otherwise.<br /> <br /> As out of pace with the current world as it is, WoD still has a lot of traction. And while the QoL changes in WoD20 to date are mostly welcome, I think the <i>mechanics</i> did deserve a new edition after WoD20 was complete. I'd be wary of any metaplot advance, but the game surely could use new rules that are actually good for a change.<br /> <br /> Some lines can particularly benefit of this. the Big Three VWM have been explored to exhaustion, but other lines still had a lot of room for exploration and fans that really wanted to see it happen.<br /> <br /> Now, in my opinion a proper continuation past-End Times would fit well in this idea of new games. Paradox's most glaring mistake was to not really commit to following through with the End Times scenarios and build whole new games using the old lore, but based on new ideas.<br /> <br /> Other than that... as I said, that's CoD. It's a good game. Actually, a great game. Unfortunately, it's also the living proof that people don't want a new game, they want WoD, and I don't think making a New New WoD will change this unless it is somehow a continuation of the cWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, CoD is when the people who did WoD do a new WoD. I'm talking about when a grown-up fan group does their own thing. And, of course, if you want V:tM proliferation levels, you need a V:tM-level cultural zeitgeist to do the astronomical amount of pulling that's required to even come close to matching D&amp;D's cultural cache.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T23:15:39-07:00","id":1554120,"title":"","content":"Well to answer the above question. WtE is kinda like that. The lore is based on BnS version and is a bit of the period peace. Since The setting presumed that the apocalypse almost happened sometime in the 80s and the main narrative through line is how the nation rebuilds after that. And even then the book is written so a st can treat it as a follow-up to w20 and for all intents and proposes wte is intended to be a new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T15:37:38-07:00","id":1554131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1554120#post1554120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well to answer the above question. WtE is kinda like that. The lore is based on BnS version and is a bit of the period peace. Since The setting presumed that the apocalypse almost happened sometime in the 80s and the main narrative through line is how the nation rebuilds after that. And even then the book is written so a st can treat it as a follow-up to w20 and for all intents and proposes wte is intended to be a new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, see, when I mean a &quot;new WoD&quot;, I mean an entirely independent, new setting that reflects the new peoples' vision, values, and what they find entertaining. WtE is absolutely not that at all, because it's still squatting in W:tA's back yard. Apologies for not being completely clear about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T20:49:47-07:00","id":1554136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1554131#post1554131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, see, when I mean a &quot;new WoD&quot;, I mean an entirely independent, new setting that reflects the new peoples' vision, values, and what they find entertaining. WtE is absolutely not that at all, because it's still squatting in W:tA's back yard. Apologies for not being completely clear about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>True a Parthfinder equivalent for wod is possible. Hell cruseborne is explicitly that. Not to mention J. F. Sambrano own totally not wta project.<br /> <br /> Though that assumes that said project is a) can distinguish itself from its inspiration and b) iecome popular in its own right. <br /> <br /> as far as I know Parthfinder is a exception and simullar projects has fallen into obscurety and/or negatively gain a stigma of being a copy like what's happening with Chronicles/new world of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T23:45:12-07:00","id":1554139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1554136#post1554136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True a Parthfinder equivalent for wod is possible. Hell cruseborne is explicitly that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't, because its creative pool was taken by people who officially worked on WoD and CoD, some of whom go way, way back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to mention J. F. Sambrano own totally not wta project.<br /> <br /> Though that assumes that said project is a) can distinguish itself from its inspiration and b) iecome popular in its own right.<br /> <br /> as far as I know Parthfinder is a exception and simullar projects has fallen into obscurety and/or negatively gain a stigma of being a copy like what's happening with Chronicles/new world of darkness. </div> </div> </div>I think that different people who didn't work on the original can probably find a way to distinguish themselves. It might not catch on, but that's the downside of media juggernauts. See also, why D&amp;D is still most of all rpg market share and Star Wars is pervasive and strangles out a lot of other sci-fi, even though it was just George Lucas making his totally not Buck Rogers because good luck getting that license (with some samurai movies and other influences on the side, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T15:43:41-07:00","id":1554178,"title":"","content":"So is it a bad thing that I want w6 to turn around and say that the Get/cult was actally the true heros all along and every bad thing they did was done by rouges packs or desgised bsds? <br /> <br /> Even if that change would elect some stong reactions from W5 crowd and w20 crowd tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T02:49:27-07:00","id":1554193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1554069#post1554069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Original WtA is already far more optimistic than most WoD to begin with, as it has the possibility of an actual victory baked in, but setting this apart...<br /> <br /> How does this really solves anything? I can see how it creates an interesting new setting that can be considered an inheritor of the old setting, but how does it actually gives either pre-5 or W5 fans a game they want to play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the thing is that I dont care for w5 fans I just want w20 back.Or if that impssoble something close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T01:04:10-07:00","id":1554401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1554178#post1554178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is it a bad thing that I want w6 to turn around and say that the Get/cult was actally the true heros all along and every bad thing they did was done by rouges packs or desgised bsds?<br /> <br /> Even if that change would elect some stong reactions from W5 crowd and w20 crowd tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you manage to appease the new fans as much... yes, yes it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551850-albrecht-s-inferno?p=1554193#post1554193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the thing is that I dont care for w5 fans I just want w20 back.Or if that impssoble something close.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, that's doing the exact same thing Paradox did with W5.<br /> <br /> I think reviving W20 is good and well, as far as it's needed to begin with. I don't like W5, I like W20 (and I've been playing WtA since 2nd edition).<br /> <br /> But if your take on it is &quot;I don't care about those fans, I'll just do what I want to play&quot;, you'll most probably end up with some stinky BS that a lot of people don't like, because <b>you</b> think you're being truer to the setting, but you're just exchanging their notion of <i>badwrongfun</i> for <b>your notion</b> of <i>badwrongfun</i>\u200b.<br /> <br /> That's why I think this whole exercise is of terrible taste. This is already exactly what you're doing: assuming that the W5 setting shouldn't be taken at face value for a new edition and anyone doing it is playing wrong, the right way is to not only throw everything away, but smear it as much as possible along the way. That's hypocritical to say the least.<br /> <br /> Your preferred game already exists, and in this I understand <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> completely. WtA is an old game, for an old time, but if you want to play it just do it. The books are there and they won't go anywhere. Unless you specifically want new books for some reason, the fact is that there's a helluva lot of books to work with, from four editions of the game.<br /> <br /> Me? I actually want a new edition because I do want better rules than the old WoD rules, but for the same setting. That could be a W20-2 or a W35 or whatever, it doesn't have to be W6. If a W6 does comes, I do prefer it comes by someone that won't act like a childish asshole the way Paradox acted and instead pays attention to the current fanbase. If we can have both games, all the better.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}